<title>UK: Lonrho may float UK car distributor - paper.</title>
<headline>Lonrho may float UK car distributor - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lonrho Plc may float its UK motor distributor Dutton-Forshaw Group, the Financial Times reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the conglomerate's chief executive Nicholas Morrell said that Dutton-Forshaw had a future as an independent public company, although he gave no further details.</p>
<p>The report said a question mark has hung over the distributor, which includes Jack Barclay -- the world's largest Bentley and Rolls-Royce dealership -- since Lonrho said last year it planned to focus on mining activities.</p>
</text>
